Subject: [PATCH] Backhaul reconnect: one attempt per scanned candidate

After a backhaul link loss the extender tries each candidate of its last
scan twice, 7 to 8 s per attempt, before scanning again. A parent that has
itself lost its uplink quiesces its backhaul BSS (0037) and never answers,
yet a scan taken right after the RF change still lists it. With four such
candidates one pass took 60 s; a parent that recovered meanwhile was found
only by the next scan (seen: extender_3 without backhaul for 80 s in the
backhaul-branch-formation room, its new parent ready after 30 s).

Try each scanned candidate once; one that did not connect is tried again
after the next scan, which also shows which parents beacon. Explicit
new-parent and last-parent transitions keep STA_MAX_CONNECT_ATTEMPT.
Admission, RSSI preference and the per-attempt timeout are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/source/core/services/vap_svc.h
+++ b/source/core/services/vap_svc.h
@@ -57,6 +57,9 @@
 //sta connection 10 seconds retry
 #define STA_CONN_RETRY_TIMEOUT                 9
 #define STA_MAX_CONNECT_ATTEMPT                2
+/* attempts per candidate of one scan before scanning again (explicit new/last
+ * parent transitions keep STA_MAX_CONNECT_ATTEMPT) */
+#define STA_MAX_SCAN_CANDIDATE_ATTEMPT         1
 #define STA_MAX_DISCONNECT_ATTEMPT             2
 #define MAX_SCAN_RESULT_WAIT                   2
 // max connection algoritham timeout 4 minutes
--- a/source/core/services/vap_svc_mesh_ext.c
+++ b/source/core/services/vap_svc_mesh_ext.c
@@ -1118,7 +1118,7 @@
 
         for (i = 0; i < ext->candidates_list.scan_count; i++) {
             if (temp == NULL && (candidate->conn_attempt == connection_attempt_wait) &&
-                (candidate->conn_retry_attempt < STA_MAX_CONNECT_ATTEMPT)) {
+                (candidate->conn_retry_attempt < STA_MAX_SCAN_CANDIDATE_ATTEMPT)) {
                 temp = candidate;
             }
             if (new_bss == NULL &&
@@ -2355,7 +2355,7 @@
         } else if (ext->conn_state == connection_state_connection_in_progress) {
             candidate = ext->candidates_list.scan_list;
             for (i = 0; i < ext->candidates_list.scan_count; i++) {
-                if ((candidate->conn_attempt == connection_attempt_wait) && (candidate->conn_retry_attempt < STA_MAX_CONNECT_ATTEMPT)) {
+                if ((candidate->conn_attempt == connection_attempt_wait) && (candidate->conn_retry_attempt < STA_MAX_SCAN_CANDIDATE_ATTEMPT)) {
                     found_candidate = true;
                     break;
                 }
